<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Stralsund</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Stralsund is a port city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecklenburg-vorpommern">Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, on the Strelasund opposite the island of Rügen. Granted town rights in 1234 by Prince Wizlaw I of Rügen, it became one of the leading Hanseatic towns and gave its name to the Treaty of Stralsund of 1370, which marked the league's victory over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a>. It withstood Wallenstein's siege in 1628 and was Swedish until 1815.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/stralsund.jpg" alt="Stralsund" width="320" height="211" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Moahim · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:WLM_-_2020_-_Stralsund_-_St._Nikolai_Kirche.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
